## Async / Background Processing

Current approach only.

Examples:

### None Yet

```text
No background processing yet.
```

### Database-backed Worker

```text
Producer writes pending tasks to database.
Worker polls/reads pending tasks and processes them asynchronously.
```

### Queue-based Processing

```text
Producer publishes messages to queue/topic.
Workers consume messages asynchronously.
```

Examples:

* AWS SQS + Lambda / ECS worker
* Google Pub/Sub + Cloud Run / Functions
* Azure Service Bus + Azure Functions
* RabbitMQ
* Kafka

Use async processing only when synchronous request/response is no longer sufficient.

Avoid premature distributed-system complexity.

